ys passes, satisfying the PRD checklist without verifying grounding.\",\"passed\":false},{\"title\":\"primaryTable fallback may emit invalid verify paths\",\"citation\":\"app-builder/src/lib/prd/sections/slices.ts:136\",\"detail\":\"isSearchFilter verify uses `tests/${primaryTable || 'collection'}-search.spec.ts`. When primaryTable is empty, the command targets collection-search.spec.ts; when primaryTable is set to a multi-word or non-slug form elsewhere, the path may not match what the generator will actually create. Combined with features.ts collectionLabel falling back to 'records', slice verify, feature e2e names, and scaffold file names can diverge. Not proven broken without the full generator, but the triple of 'records' / 'collection' / primaryTable is inconsistent within this patch alone.\",\"passed\":false},{\"title\":\"Definition-of-Done self-check strength not fully visible in chunk\",\"citation\":\"app-builder/src/lib/prd/selfCheck.ts:193\",\"detail\":\"hasDefinitionOfDone requires DEFINITION_OF_DONE_HEADING plus every DONE_CHECKLIST_SECTIONS row id as `**id**` in markdown. That is a solid anti-stub pattern. The patch then truncates mid-items list at gate; whether definition-of-done is wired into the items array and into the overall pass aggregate is not fully shown in the visible portion after the offload cut. From what is present, search-feature and assistant-feature items are added correctly. No explicit fail on incomplete wiring can be proven from the visible lines only—do not pass the full selfCheck change as verified beyond the visible hasSearchFeature/hasAssistantFeature and hasDefinitionOfDone computations.\",\"passed\":false},{\"title\":\"Home forgeResult error path improves fail-closed UX\",\"citation\":\"app-builder/src/pages/Home.tsx:175\",\"detail\":\"generatePrd failures are caught, including UnresolvedPrdError, and surface ErrorBanner with back-to-wizard / new actions instead of leaving prd null with a silent empty result. That matches f
